# Code owners for NKE Recipes.
#
# GitHub requests review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so the default is declared first and the
# trust roots override it below.
#
# The principle: anything that determines WHAT GETS BUILT, WHAT IS TRUSTED, or
# WHAT RUNS IN CI requires maintainer review. Ordinary implementation does not.
#
# Roles are defined in GOVERNANCE.md. Both teams must hold write access to this
# repository or GitHub silently ignores the entry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — all trusted contributors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*                                       @NVIDIA/nke-write

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trust roots — maintainer review required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The lock contract (ADR-22). A lock entry is the exact content identity of
# something that will be built and published; changing one changes what ships.
/definitions/**/catalog/pins.lock.yaml  @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# The registry: which components exist and their constraints. Paired with the
# lock above under ADR-22's registry/lockfile split.
/definitions/**/catalog/registry.yaml   @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# Definition and Environment are Tier-1 inputs bound into `recipeDigest`
# (ADR-11, ADR-12). A change here changes recipe identity.
/definitions/**/definition.yaml         @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/definitions/**/environment-*.yaml      @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# Toolchain pins. A toolchain digest is a build-semantic input (ADR-10 §5) and
# contaminates every artifact built with it.
/toolchains/**/*.lock.json              @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# The design record. ADRs govern design and are what a change is reviewed
# against; amending one is amending the contract.
/docs/adr/                              @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# CI, workflows, and repository automation. This is the code that decides what
# "passing" means, plus the generated Run pipeline and its plan.
/.github/                               @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# The CI contract: `make check` is what CI runs, so a Makefile change changes
# the gate.
/Makefile                               @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# Dependency surface. CONTRIBUTING names Apache-cleanliness a load-bearing
# invariant, and it is enforced here by review until a license gate exists.
/go.mod                                 @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/go.sum                                 @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer

# Licensing, security policy, governance, and this file.
/LICENSE                                @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/SECURITY.md                            @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/GOVERNANCE.md                          @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/MAINTAINERS.md                         @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                     @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @NVIDIA/nke-maintainer
